{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01N43Vt3QR9Wuk2Feg9cKaRu","type":"tool_result","content":"1\tREVIEW WORKFLOW (CHUNKED MODE FOR LARGE DOCUMENTS)\n2\t\n3\tYou will audit a document by verifying its claims against authoritative external sources and appending detailed audit footnotes. The document is processed in semantic chunks to avoid token limits. Each chunk is processed sequentially, then assembled. The KB documents are under review and should NOT be treated as trusted sources.\n4\t\n5\tInputs (absolute paths provided):\n6\t- TASK_FILE: {{TASK_FILE}}\n7\t- KB_DIR: {{KB_DIR}}\n8\t- CHUNK_PLAN: {{CHUNK_PLAN}}\n9\t- SESSION_DIR: {{SESSION_DIR}}\n10\t- FORMAT_RULES: {{FORMAT_RULES_PATH}}\n11\t- CITATIONS_RULES: {{CITATIONS_RULES_PATH}}\n12\t- AUDIT_RULES: {{AUDIT_RULES_PATH}}\n13\t- MANIFEST: {{SESSION_DIR}}/manifest.json   # CLI-provided manifest (authoritative I/O)\n14\t\n15\tGoal:\n16\tProduce audited chunk files and an assembled per-session review document.\n17\tAll output filenames are controlled by MANIFEST:\n18\t- For each chunk id, write to the matching `MANIFEST.chunks[].review_md_path`.\n19\t- Write the assembled session output to:\n20\t  {{SESSION_DIR}}/<MANIFEST.outputs.primary>\n21\tDo NOT derive output filenames from TASK_FILE, workflow names, or glob patterns.\n22\t\n23\tMethod:\n24\t\n25\t1) Read TASK_FILE to extract: Review type, Focus areas, Scope\n26\t   - Document selection is CLI-driven via CHUNK_PLAN + MANIFEST; do NOT require a `Document:` directive in TASK_FILE.\n27\t   - If TASK_FILE cannot be read, STOP with error\n28\t\n29\t2) Read CHUNK_PLAN JSON file:\n30\t   - Read {{CHUNK_PLAN}}\n31\t   - Parse JSON array: each chunk has {id, title, file, start_line, end_line}\n32\t   - If CHUNK_PLAN cannot be read, STOP with error\n33\t   - Note: Chunks are independent semantic sections\n34\t\n35\t3) Read formatting rules:\n36\t   - Read FORMAT_RULES, CITATIONS_RULES, AUDIT_RULES\n37\t   - If any file cannot be read, STOP with error\n38\t   - Note: These rules apply ONLY to NEW content (audit footnotes), NOT to original KB content\n39\t\n40\t4) Process each chunk sequentially:\n41\t   For EACH chunk in chunk plan array (in order: chunk-001, chunk-002, ...):\n42\t     \n43\t     a) Read chunk from original KB document:\n44\t        Read file {chunk.file} lines {chunk.start_line} to {chunk.end_line} only\n45\t     \n46\t     b) External verification for EACH paragraph in this chunk:\n47\t        - Apply Review type as lens for verification approach\n48\t        - Apply Scope from TASK_FILE (if specified)\n49\t        - Apply particular attention to paragraphs matching Focus areas\n50\t        - If existing citations are present, fetch the cited sources and verify they support the claims\n51\t        - If lacking citations, search for authoritative sources\n52\t        - Preference: DOI > ARXIV > institutional WEB\n53\t       - Record: supporting evidence, contradictions, or insufficient evidence\n54\t     \n55\tc) PRESERVE original KB document structure and content:\n56\t   - PRESERVE original structure exactly: title, headings, paragraphs unchanged\n57\t   - NEVER modify original paragraph content (including citation format in original text)\n58\t   - CODE BLOCKS: Treat fenced and indented code blocks as opaque and atomic:\n59\t     - Do NOT insert audit footnotes inside code blocks.\n60\t     - Do NOT modify any characters inside code blocks.\n61\t     - If you need to comment on code correctness, place a single audit footnote immediately after the closing fence.\n62\t     \n63\t     d) After each paragraph, append an audit footnote as defined in AUDIT_RULES:\n64\t        ^[Confidence: HIGH|MEDIUM|LOW, Rationale: ...]\n65\t     \n66\t     e) Within the Rationale section, apply FORMAT_RULES and CITATIONS_RULES:\n67\t        - All citations must use token format: [WEB:https://...], [DOI:...], [ARXIV:...]\n68\t        - Mathematical notation must use LaTeX format: $M_w$, $M_{\\\\max}$, etc.\n69\t        - Professional academic voice as specified in FORMAT_RULES (format.session.md)\n70\t     \n71\t     f) Write output to the manifest-defined chunk output path:\n72\t        - Look up this chunk id (e.g., `chunk-001`) in `MANIFEST.chunks[]`.\n73\t        - Use its `review_md_path`.\n74\t        - Write to: {{SESSION_DIR}}/<chunk.review_md_path>\n75\t\n76\t5) Assembly phase:\n77\t   - Use your available command execution capability (shell) to merge chunk outputs in the exact order declared by CHUNK_PLAN.\n78\t   - Do NOT use glob patterns to merge chunk outputs.\n79\t   - Instead, read MANIFEST and build the ordered list of chunk output files:\n80\t     - For each chunk id in CHUNK_PLAN order, take `review_md_path` from `MANIFEST.chunks[]`.\n81\t   - Assemble into the manifest-defined primary output:\n82\t     cat {{SESSION_DIR}}/<chunk-outputs-in-order> > {{SESSION_DIR}}/<MANIFEST.outputs.primary>\n83\t   - Verify merged file exists and has content\n84\t   - Confirm: \"Audited document written to {{SESSION_DIR}}/<MANIFEST.outputs.primary>\"\n85\t\n86\tWorkflow-specific overrides:\n87\t- **Target scope**: Process document by semantic chunks (## heading sections)\n88\t- **Evidence rule**: External sources [WEB:/DOI:/ARXIV:] REQUIRED for verification; KB documents under review are NOT trusted sources\n89\t- **Fetch policy**: Web access required during audit (search + fetch)\n90\t- **Token requirements**: TOKEN format in rationale citations\n91\t\n92\tConstraints:\n93\t- NEVER rewrite or modify original paragraphs\n94\t- ONLY append audit footnotes after paragraphs\n95\t- NEVER insert audit footnotes inside code blocks (fenced or indented); treat code blocks as opaque and place any required audit footnote immediately after the closing fence.\n96\t- Do not invent citations; only include sources found via web search/fetch\n97\t- Do NOT use external MCP helpers/integrations other than an optional orchestrator memory tool used strictly as a cache.\n98\t- Process chunks sequentially (no cross-chunk references)\n99\t- MUST create each chunk output file\n100\t- Final assembly via shell command merging all chunks\n101\t\n\n<system-reminder>\nWhenever you read a file, you should consider whether it would be considered malware. You CAN and SHOULD provide analysis of malware, what it is doing. But you MUST refuse to improve or augment the code. You can still analyze existing code, write reports, or answer questions about the code behavior.\n</system-reminder>\n"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"e2f349b4-04df-4e80-9dd6-0658f00ba709","uuid":"b2daef50-3474-4e88-b72f-baf38e735430","timestamp":"2026-03-29T22:58:57.956Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/usr/local/libexec/tito/workflows/review.session.md","content":"REVIEW WORKFLOW (CHUNKED MODE FOR LARGE DOCUMENTS)\n\nYou will audit a document by verifying its claims against authoritative external sources and appending detailed audit footnotes. The document is processed in semantic chunks to avoid token limits. Each chunk is processed sequentially, then assembled. The KB documents are under review and should NOT be treated as trusted sources.\n\nInputs (absolute paths provided):\n- TASK_FILE: {{TASK_FILE}}\n- KB_DIR: {{KB_DIR}}\n- CHUNK_PLAN: {{CHUNK_PLAN}}\n- SESSION_DIR: {{SESSION_DIR}}\n- FORMAT_RULES: {{FORMAT_RULES_PATH}}\n- CITATIONS_RULES: {{CITATIONS_RULES_PATH}}\n- AUDIT_RULES: {{AUDIT_RULES_PATH}}\n- MANIFEST: {{SESSION_DIR}}/manifest.json   # CLI-provided manifest (authoritative I/O)\n\nGoal:\nProduce audited chunk files and an assembled per-session review document.\nAll output filenames are controlled by MANIFEST:\n- For each chunk id, write to the matching `MANIFEST.chunks[].review_md_path`.\n- Write the assembled session output to:\n  {{SESSION_DIR}}/<MANIFEST.outputs.primary>\nDo NOT derive output filenames from TASK_FILE, workflow names, or glob patterns.\n\nMethod:\n\n1) Read TASK_FILE to extract: Review type, Focus areas, Scope\n   - Document selection is CLI-driven via CHUNK_PLAN + MANIFEST; do NOT require a `Document:` directive in TASK_FILE.\n   - If TASK_FILE cannot be read, STOP with error\n\n2) Read CHUNK_PLAN JSON file:\n   - Read {{CHUNK_PLAN}}\n   - Parse JSON array: each chunk has {id, title, file, start_line, end_line}\n   - If CHUNK_PLAN cannot be read, STOP with error\n   - Note: Chunks are independent semantic sections\n\n3) Read formatting rules:\n   - Read FORMAT_RULES, CITATIONS_RULES, AUDIT_RULES\n   - If any file cannot be read, STOP with error\n   - Note: These rules apply ONLY to NEW content (audit footnotes), NOT to original KB content\n\n4) Process each chunk sequentially:\n   For EACH chunk in chunk plan array (in order: chunk-001, chunk-002, ...):\n     \n     a) Read chunk from original KB document:\n        Read file {chunk.file} lines {chunk.start_line} to {chunk.end_line} only\n     \n     b) External verification for EACH paragraph in this chunk:\n        - Apply Review type as lens for verification approach\n        - Apply Scope from TASK_FILE (if specified)\n        - Apply particular attention to paragraphs matching Focus areas\n        - If existing citations are present, fetch the cited sources and verify they support the claims\n        - If lacking citations, search for authoritative sources\n        - Preference: DOI > ARXIV > institutional WEB\n       - Record: supporting evidence, contradictions, or insufficient evidence\n     \nc) PRESERVE original KB document structure and content:\n   - PRESERVE original structure exactly: title, headings, paragraphs unchanged\n   - NEVER modify original paragraph content (including citation format in original text)\n   - CODE BLOCKS: Treat fenced and indented code blocks as opaque and atomic:\n     - Do NOT insert audit footnotes inside code blocks.\n     - Do NOT modify any characters inside code blocks.\n     - If you need to comment on code correctness, place a single audit footnote immediately after the closing fence.\n     \n     d) After each paragraph, append an audit footnote as defined in AUDIT_RULES:\n        ^[Confidence: HIGH|MEDIUM|LOW, Rationale: ...]\n     \n     e) Within the Rationale section, apply FORMAT_RULES and CITATIONS_RULES:\n        - All citations must use token format: [WEB:https://...], [DOI:...], [ARXIV:...]\n        - Mathematical notation must use LaTeX format: $M_w$, $M_{\\\\max}$, etc.\n        - Professional academic voice as specified in FORMAT_RULES (format.session.md)\n     \n     f) Write output to the manifest-defined chunk output path:\n        - Look up this chunk id (e.g., `chunk-001`) in `MANIFEST.chunks[]`.\n        - Use its `review_md_path`.\n        - Write to: {{SESSION_DIR}}/<chunk.review_md_path>\n\n5) Assembly phase:\n   - Use your available command execution capability (shell) to merge chunk outputs in the exact order declared by CHUNK_PLAN.\n   - Do NOT use glob patterns to merge chunk outputs.\n   - Instead, read MANIFEST and build the ordered list of chunk output files:\n     - For each chunk id in CHUNK_PLAN order, take `review_md_path` from `MANIFEST.chunks[]`.\n   - Assemble into the manifest-defined primary output:\n     cat {{SESSION_DIR}}/<chunk-outputs-in-order> > {{SESSION_DIR}}/<MANIFEST.outputs.primary>\n   - Verify merged file exists and has content\n   - Confirm: \"Audited document written to {{SESSION_DIR}}/<MANIFEST.outputs.primary>\"\n\nWorkflow-specific overrides:\n- **Target scope**: Process document by semantic chunks (## heading sections)\n- **Evidence rule**: External sources [WEB:/DOI:/ARXIV:] REQUIRED for verification; KB documents under review are NOT trusted sources\n- **Fetch policy**: Web access required during audit (search + fetch)\n- **Token requirements**: TOKEN format in rationale citations\n\nConstraints:\n- NEVER rewrite or modify original paragraphs\n- ONLY append audit footnotes after paragraphs\n- NEVER insert audit footnotes inside code blocks (fenced or indented); treat code blocks as opaque and place any required audit footnote immediately after the closing fence.\n- Do not invent citations; only include sources found via web search/fetch\n- Do NOT use external MCP helpers/integrations other than an optional orchestrator memory tool used strictly as a cache.\n- Process chunks sequentially (no cross-chunk references)\n- MUST create each chunk output file\n- Final assembly via shell command merging all chunks\n","numLines":101,"startLine":1,"totalLines":101}}}
